<title>UK: BASF SEES BROAD EMU STARTING ON TIME.</title>
<headline>BASF SEES BROAD EMU STARTING ON TIME.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>German chemicals group BASF AG chairman Juergen Strube said on Thursday that he expects European Monetary Union (EMU) to start on time.</p>
<p>&quot;I expect EMU to start on schedule and to be broadly based,&quot; he told a news conference here.</p>
<p>Strube acknowledged that many Germans were concerned about the creation of a single currency and the loss of the mark but said that European business, &quot;is quite clearly in favour of EMU.&quot;</p>
<p>&quot;I hope that we will see some progress in convincing  the electors that this is the right way to move,&quot; Strube said.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
